--- An answer of no value handed on says nothing of the parameter it
--- reaches: an early round's answer of a function whose first return is
--- an error, narrowed by its guard, had made a copy of magpie's `place`
--- whose bytes were no value, and the flush that later handed bytes
--- reached that copy — an internal error (crow check --self, `merge` of a
--- parsed value). The program stops alike in both modes, at the text the
--- log's directory had to be.
use magpie

log['merging a parsed value']
log[magpie.merge[json['{"a": 1}'], true]]
log['not reached']
